{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/590415-rolling-for-detachment-when-to-do-it","id":590415,"title":"Rolling for Detachment: When to do it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-14T12:57:11-07:00","id":590415,"title":"Rolling for Detachment: When to do it?","content":"Something I've been wondering about is when you guys time your detachment rolls. Do you do it at the end of the scene, based upon the worst &quot;sin&quot; committed? Or do you instead do it the moment it occurs, and possibly make multiple rolls in a scene? Do you hand out a beat for every risk in the scene?<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear people's play experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:14:18-07:00","id":590442,"title":"","content":"I usually wait for the end of the scene, if not of the session. The more I wait, the more I use situational modifiers and a special penalty for number of &quot;sins&quot; to compensate for the wait. But it does depend a lot on the chronicle. Since I do a variety of games, not every one demands the same approach. The more Integrity is a relevant theme of te current game, the less I wait.<br /> <br /> But when I do it at the moment, I prefer to make it more than a roll. I make a little &quot;mental&quot; scene, an internal monologue where everyone can ask questions about the thoughts of the character about what he done. It's a short scene, but is crucial to set the tone of the game. IF Integrity is a central theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:58:42-07:00","id":590465,"title":"","content":"I generally do it as the potentially detaching event or decision happens - although I should also say I haven't asked for a lot of Detachment rolls, not even as many as one per session on average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T18:16:06-07:00","id":590664,"title":"","content":"At the time, unless it'll break the flow of whatever's going on, in which case we'll do it at the end of the game or during a break, though I'll probably describe a sense of tension in its place.<br /> <br /> I've done multiple rolls in the scene for the same character, but it's something I'd save for particularly dramatic moments and choices from the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T18:43:01-07:00","id":590673,"title":"","content":"I do it at the end of the scene. I factor the biggest detachment issue, then add a -1, -2, or -3 penalty for further points of detachment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T19:56:46-07:00","id":590715,"title":"","content":"I'm lucky if my players hit a breaking point in half a dozen scenes, so I have no real set-in-stone preferences, myself. Usually I do it when I remember it, but no earlier than at the end of the current bit of action (not in the middle of combat, for example, but at the end of it), but not always at the end of a scene.<br /> <br /> If I weren't so forgetful, I'd probably try to do it whenever the PC has a moment to think and register what they did, since the roll is meant to represent how they react to their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T05:17:34-07:00","id":591156,"title":"","content":"During play, I only tell the players that they have just experienced a breaking point at the end of the scene (mostly so they can note the Beat they're getting for it on their sheets). I keep track of the breaking points on a piece of paper.<br /> The detachment rolls happen at the end of the chapter. I play wrap-up scenes with Touchstones, where the characters reflect on their actions and what that means for them. These are usually quite solemn. At the end of that, I discuss situational modifiers with my players (only 2 players, mind...), based on the number and nature of breaking points they experienced and the roleplaying they put into the wrap-up scene. Then I let them roll for their worst breaking point with all those situational modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T08:10:00-07:00","id":591338,"title":"","content":"I do it at the next &quot;sequel&quot;, that is, when the characters have time to reflect over what just happened. Sometimes this happens directly after a scene that triggered the Breaking Point, sometimes it takes a little while. A few times, I've even had to delay it from one session to the next due to how late it was getting, and the characters still had no chance of calming down and reflect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T13:44:10-07:00","id":593108,"title":"","content":"I have them roll at the end of the scene, sometimes my players even suggest it or point it out for a diffferent player if something horrible has happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}